WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:02.690
Speaker 1: Let's go to Aaron from Los Angeles.

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:04.450
Aaron, welcome to the show.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.341
Speaker 5: I did it.

00:00:06.341 --> 00:00:12.239
I just wanted to ask a quick question regarding
I guess, I don't know, intellectual copyright

00:00:12.239 --> 00:00:17.199
is the term, but there's been like I've been
reading a lot of articles regarding, I guess

00:00:17.199 --> 00:00:18.199
like Bill Gates.

00:00:18.199 --> 00:00:21.189
And just to be clear, I am not an anti-vaxxer,
okay?

00:00:21.189 --> 00:00:24.470
I mean, like I'm triple VAX boosted and everything.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:29.029
So before I go into this, I just want to say
that I understand that Bill Gates is a source

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:33.649
of a controversy when it becomes, I guess,
like intellectual property and copyright,

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:38.350
like he has been getting involved in a scandal
regarding vaccines not being distributed to

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:41.090
the global south as quickly as they should
be.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:45.040
And a lot of people are identifying this as
a major reason the COVID 19 pandemic isn't

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.129
slowing down.

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:52.370
I was wondering, what could our Congress do
to perhaps reform our intellectual copyright

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:57.649
laws to prevent, I guess, big pharmaceutical
companies from preventing, you know, necessary

00:00:57.649 --> 00:00:59.059
access to vaccines?

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:09.390
Speaker 1: Well, with it with vaccines specifically,
the desire has been for the vaccines to to

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:16.700
essentially not be protected by copyright
or intellectual property, patent protections,

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:21.090
and just to be basically allowed to be open
sourced and produced anywhere.

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:25.670
And there was a brief period where Moderna
said, we still have our patent, but we're

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:28.030
not necessarily going to enforce it.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:31.310
And know I don't know ultimately what happened
with that.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:35.700
There's a number of different issues going
on with vaccine distribution, but I just I'm

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.170
not exactly sure.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:41.610
With vaccines specifically, it's one set of
problems.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:46.860
Bigger picture, there is all sorts of other
intellectual property issues that that exist

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.860
and would be dealt with in different ways.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:51.470
So I'm just I'm just not sure how to address
the question.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:53.180
Speaker 5: Okay.

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:54.180
Yeah.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.410
It's just I know that Bill Gates has been
tied up with intellectual property rights

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:01.082
even since, like his foundation of Microsoft
in the 1990s.

00:02:01.082 --> 00:02:06.190
I mean, as a matter of fact, before he was
getting into philanthropy, a lot of the controversies

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:10.240
that he had regarding Microsoft's monopoly
on the software industry were really one of

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:11.470
the things that he was best known for.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:16.239
Speaker 1: Yeah, there was the big issue about
the bundling of Internet Explorer with windows

00:02:16.239 --> 00:02:22.599
in which he gave, you know, hours and hours
of pretty, pretty notable depositions.

00:02:22.599 --> 00:02:24.359
And yeah, you're absolutely right.

00:02:24.359 --> 00:02:28.489
But to be perfectly frank, I don't know that
Bill Gates is the biggest player right now

00:02:28.489 --> 00:02:30.480
in what's going on with vaccines.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:31.909
Speaker 5: Okay.

00:02:31.909 --> 00:02:32.909
I understand.

00:02:32.909 --> 00:02:33.909
Yeah.

00:02:33.909 --> 00:02:35.260
Yeah, I know that.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:39.930
It's just like in regards to his philanthropy,
I understand that he does have a lot of influence

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.069
with it.

00:02:41.069 --> 00:02:45.299
I just think that, like, maybe the extent
could be overstated as a result of, like,

00:02:45.299 --> 00:02:48.190
you know, the various conspiracy theories
that are around him right now.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:51.629
But I guess that is just something I would
look into.

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:56.799
It's just I honestly just think that if we
don't slow down the effects of the COVID 19

00:02:56.799 --> 00:03:00.150
pandemic in the global south, we're going
to continue to see these variants.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:03.849
And I don't really I don't know if it's going
to lead to another shutdown, but I do think

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:05.790
it's definitely going to lead to the spread
of the infection.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:06.840
Speaker 1: Yep.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:12.439
And we're seeing cases go up now and hopefully
it won't become a major spike, but a point.

00:03:12.439 --> 00:03:14.049
Well said and well-taken.

00:03:14.049 --> 00:03:16.439
I appreciate the call very much.

00:03:16.439 --> 00:03:18.950
Glad we could speak to a few people today.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:24.650
Thanks to our guest bailing on us, we'll still
take the broader calls for our Friday show.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.980
We'll take a quick break and be back right
after this.

